    "media:imagetext": "315 Montgomezy Street\nSen Francisco\nSeptember 23, 1929\nLt. Col. Gezela C, Brandt\nGrissy Field\nSen 7zene1soo, Californie.\nMy dear Colonel Brandt:\nAs a 2esult of the conference of our Cormittee a\nLew days ago, I en sending three copies of the joint\nreport of our Cormittee to you.\nI w111 esk that you and\nMn, Mouton sign each of these three copies and thet you\nme11 the original to 1110H, Kent, Cheirman of the Airport\nConnittee of the Board of Supervisozs,\nimmediately.\nhave already signed the three copies which I enelose to\nyou. The other two copies aze for you and im. Mouton.\nAs I will not be back fzom Burope unt11 about\nDecember 10th, I am very anxious that the Birport Committee\nof the Board of Supervisors have our full report in their\nhands, because it explains in detail,\nthe position consist-\nently\ntaken by our Advisory Comnittee.\nWith best regards and good wishes, I am\nSincerely,\n(Signed) BILI",
